	-> VPC : virtual private cloud
	
	-> subnet : used to create multiple subnets in vpc
		- can create private and public subnets
		- can access internet of private subnet using nat gateway
	
	-> internet-gateway : give internet access to vpc
	
	-> route table : can define rules for subnet's internet connection according to ip address
	
	-> create private & public subnets : 
		- create a route table with default configuration(0.0.0.0 - local) and add subnets in that table which u want to make private, means that subnet does not have internet connection
		- create a route table with igt access to 0.0.0.0 and add any subnet to that table an dit will become a public subnet because it will have internet access
		
	-> nat-instance
	
	-> nat-gateway : provide internet to private instance which is in private subnet using public subnet
		- had to add nat-gateway in private route table's routes (edit route)
	
	-> NACL - network access control list 
		- used to block the access from specific ip address 
		- security group can only allow the traffic, can't deny but nacl can deny the incoming call from specific ip address
		
